OHIRA-0007

CLI & Developer Experience Specification

Project: Ohira

Document ID: OHIRA-0007

Version: 1.0

Status: Founder's Draft


---

Purpose

The Ohira Command Line Interface (CLI) is the primary interface between developers and the Ohira platform.

It should be:

Fast

Simple

Discoverable

Scriptable

Consistent

AI-friendly


The CLI should feel like a natural part of a developer's workflow, similar to tools like Git, Docker, Prisma, and npm.


---

Design Principles

Developer First

Every command should solve a real developer problem with minimal configuration.


---

Convention Over Configuration

Ohira should detect common project structures automatically.

Example:

ohira analyze

No configuration should be required for most projects.


---

Human + Machine Friendly

Every command supports multiple output formats:

ohira status

ohira status --json

ohira status --yaml

ohira status --markdown


---

Installation

Global installation:

pnpm add -g ohira

or

npm install -g ohira

or

bun add -g ohira

No lock-in to a single package manager.


---

Initialization

Initialize a project:

ohira init

Creates:

.ohira/
    config.json
    cache/
    reports/
    graph/


---

Configuration

Configuration file:

ohira.config.ts

Example:

export default {
  project: {
    name: "Smart Property",
    description: "AI-first PropTech Platform"
  },

  plugins: [
    "prisma",
    "next",
    "docker",
    "clerk"
  ],

  output: {
    reports: "./reports"
  }
}


---

Core Commands

Analyze

ohira analyze

Runs:

Scanner

Collectors

Plugins

Knowledge Graph

Reports



---

Status

ohira status

Example output:

Project: Smart Property

Framework: Next.js

Runtime: Node.js

ORM: Prisma

Database: MySQL

Authentication: Clerk

Modules: 9

Health Score: 91%

Analysis completed in 6.2 seconds


---

Doctor

ohira doctor

Checks:

Missing dependencies

Configuration issues

Plugin compatibility

Version conflicts


Example:

✓ Node.js detected

✓ Prisma detected

✓ Docker detected

⚠ Missing plugin:
@ohira/plugin-git


---

Report

ohira report

Generates:

report.md

report.json

report.html


---

Context

ohira context

Produces AI-ready project context.


---

Graph

ohira graph

Displays a summary of the project's knowledge graph.

Future versions may support interactive visualization.


---

Plugins

List plugins:

ohira plugins list

Install:

ohira plugins install prisma

Update:

ohira plugins update

Remove:

ohira plugins remove prisma


---

Cache

ohira cache clear

Removes cached analysis.


---

Upgrade

ohira upgrade

Updates the CLI and official plugins.


---

Output Formats

Supported:

--json

--yaml

--markdown

--table

--html

This allows integration with scripts, CI/CD pipelines, and AI systems.


---

Interactive Mode

When no arguments are provided:

ohira

Display an interactive menu:

Welcome to Ohira

1. Analyze Project
2. View Status
3. Generate Report
4. AI Context
5. Plugin Manager
6. Doctor
7. Settings

This improves discoverability for new users.


---

Exit Codes

Standard exit codes:

Code	Meaning

0	Success
1	General error
2	Invalid command
3	Configuration error
4	Plugin error
5	Analysis failed


This makes Ohira automation-friendly.


---

Logging

Levels:

--quiet

--info

--verbose

--debug

Verbose mode helps diagnose issues during development.


---

Performance Goals

CLI startup under 200 ms

Analyze medium projects in under 30 seconds

Incremental re-analysis under 5 seconds after small changes

Minimal memory usage



---

AI Commands (Future)

ohira explain

ohira summarize

ohira architecture

ohira review

ohira risks

ohira roadmap

These commands will use the Knowledge Graph to provide higher-level insights.


---

Developer Experience Goals

A new developer should be able to:

pnpm add -g ohira

cd my-project

ohira init

ohira analyze

ohira status

ohira report

and understand a project within minutes.


---

Future Enhancements

Shell auto-completion (Bash, Zsh, Fish, PowerShell)

Interactive TUI dashboard

Watch mode (ohira analyze --watch)

Live architecture updates

AI-assisted troubleshooting

Workspace management for multiple projects



---

Guiding Principle

> "Powerful by default. Flexible when needed."



The CLI should hide complexity from beginners while exposing advanced capabilities for experienced developers and automation workflows.


---

Milestone Deliverables

The CLI for Ohira v0.1 must include:

ohira init

ohira analyze

ohira status

ohira doctor

ohira report

ohira context

Basic plugin management

JSON and Markdown output

Configuration support



